# Phase 18 Netty frame-limit setting parity — 2026-10-15T11:29:59Z

- Audited the pinned Java 5.5.1 `NettyDecoder`: its class initializer reads
  `com.rocketmq.remoting.frameMaxLength` with default `16777216`. Rust had used
  a fixed 16 MiB limit and did not read the setting.
- Added first-connection resolution of the same-named process environment
  setting, Java `Integer.parseInt`-compatible signed decimal parsing, positive
  limit validation, and the Java default. Each connection retains the resolved
  value for inbound decoding and outbound request/response encoding.
- Added `fixtures/runtime/netty-frame-limit.json`, a Java probe run in separate
  default/configured JVMs, and a Rust child-process loopback test. The Rust test
  confirms a configured `4096` limit reaches a new connection and rejects an
  oversized outbound frame.
- PASS: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --locked` (84 unit, 6 codec,
  1 fuzz regression, 5 security, and 86 transport tests); strict all-target,
  all-feature Remoting Clippy; `mvn -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify`
  (37 scenarios, both frame-limit probes, Java decoding 2 Rust-generated base
  frames, 54 typed headers, and 14 typed bodies); `cargo fmt --all -- --check`;
  `git diff --check`.
- Code commit: `754d5050 fix(remoting): honor Java Netty frame limit property`.
- Updated the Phase 2 compatibility row and Phase 18 release checklist. This
  closes the frame-limit setting slice only; broad P18-V01 remains open.
- Remaining non-manual work: complete broad bidirectional P18-V01 source/API,
  setting, input/error/control-flow, inherited API and Rust reverse-export
  reconciliation; rerun all current-revision P18-V02 server-free gates after
  this commit; obtain current-revision GitHub Ubuntu address-profile evidence
  for P18-V04; and implement/run Phase 19 local Docker/Broker automation.
  Release-version confirmation and registry dependency-resolution checks also
  remain before publication. Owner-run deployment/live Broker checks remain in
  Phase 19 and are separate from these local tasks.
- The pinned Java source repository was read-only. No plan, push, tag, release,
  or Broker validation was performed.
